            <ArticleTitle>[Separation of the symphysis, an unrecognized complication of delivery. A case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Post-partum abdominal pain is common. Separation of the pubic symphysis is one cause. Diagnosis is based upon clinical and ultrasonographic findings. Bed rest is often satisfactory treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
